WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.118
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.418 --> 00:00:08.955
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.255 --> 00:00:15.367
Unit twenty-six: Was / Were (past of to be). Today you will talk about where people and things were in the past.

4
00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:18.320
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:22.790
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:24.500
Was.

7
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:27.690
Was means the past of am and is.

8
00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:29.749
I was at home yesterday.

9
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.341
Your turn. Say: Was.

10
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.131
Was.

11
00:00:36.883 --> 00:00:37.443
Were.

12
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.078
Were means the past of are.

13
00:00:40.683 --> 00:00:41.766
They were at school.

14
00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.642
Your turn. Say: Were.

15
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.443
Were.

16
00:00:49.183 --> 00:00:50.208
Yesterday.

17
00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.356
Yesterday means the day before today.

18
00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.566
I was tired yesterday.

19
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.640
Your turn. Say: Yesterday.

20
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.617
Yesterday.

21
00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:04.477
Last week.

22
00:01:05.483 --> 00:01:07.727
Last week means the week before this one.

23
00:01:08.317 --> 00:01:10.026
We were on holiday last week.

24
00:01:10.617 --> 00:01:13.246
Your turn. Say: Last week.

25
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.368
Last week.

26
00:01:18.117 --> 00:01:19.153
I was.

27
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:22.695
I was means I used to be in a place or state.

28
00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.412
I was happy.

29
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:27.356
Your turn. Say: I was.

30
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.166
I was.

31
00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:32.836
They were.

32
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.500
They were means more than one person used to be there.

33
00:01:37.083 --> 00:01:38.224
They were friends.

34
00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:41.365
Your turn. Say: They were.

35
00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.155
They were.

36
00:01:45.917 --> 00:01:46.744
Wasn't.

37
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.041
Wasn't means was not.

38
00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:50.848
She wasn't at home.

39
00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.835
Your turn. Say: Wasn't.

40
00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.539
Wasn't.

41
00:01:58.283 --> 00:01:59.064
Weren't.

42
00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.469
Weren't means were not.

43
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:03.108
We weren't late.

44
00:02:03.717 --> 00:02:05.951
Your turn. Say: Weren't.

45
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:09.697
Weren't.

46
00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.290
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:16.999
Visal, where were you yesterday?

48
00:02:18.083 --> 00:02:29.161
I was at home. Was is the past of am and is. Were is the past of are. We use was with I, he, she and it. We use were with you, we and they.

49
00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.739
How do we make negatives?

50
00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:42.256
Add not: I was not at school. They were not late. In speaking we say wasn't and weren't. She wasn't happy. We weren't there.

51
00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.548
And questions?

52
00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:57.772
Put was or were first: Were you at school? Was she tired? We answer: Yes, I was. No, she wasn't. Time words like yesterday and last week tell us it is the past.

53
00:02:58.933 --> 00:03:00.852
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.717 --> 00:03:05.342
Grammar focus: Past of be: was and were.

55
00:03:05.642 --> 00:03:06.840
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:09.143
I was at home yesterday.

57
00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.783
They were at school last week.

58
00:03:12.683 --> 00:03:14.091
She wasn't at the party.

59
00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:23.284
Use was with I, he, she and it, and were with you, we and they. Negatives: wasn't and weren't. Questions: Was she…? Were you…?

60
00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:27.445
Be careful! Don't say: We was late yesterday.

61
00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.214
Say: We were late yesterday.

62
00:03:31.514 --> 00:03:32.852
Use were with we.

63
00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:36.307
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.751
Yesterday and Last Week.

65
00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:41.875
Yesterday I was at home, and my brother was at school.

66
00:03:42.867 --> 00:03:45.923
My parents were at work, and my sister was with a friend.

67
00:03:46.933 --> 00:03:48.852
Last week we were in Siem Reap.

68
00:03:49.867 --> 00:03:52.981
The weather wasn't hot, and the hotel wasn't expensive.

69
00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:56.175
Were you on holiday last week too?

70
00:03:57.267 --> 00:04:01.559
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:02.417 --> 00:04:04.393
I blank at school yesterday.

72
00:04:04.693 --> 00:04:07.545
A, were. B, was. C, am.

73
00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.100
The answer is B: was.

74
00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:16.342
They blank in Phnom Penh last week.

75
00:04:16.642 --> 00:04:19.541
A, was. B, is. C, were.

76
00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.809
The answer is C: were.

77
00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.196
She blank happy. (negative)

78
00:04:28.496 --> 00:04:31.882
A, wasn't. B, weren't. C, isn't was.

79
00:04:35.433 --> 00:04:37.375
The answer is A: wasn't.

80
00:04:38.517 --> 00:04:40.249
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:40.549 --> 00:04:44.551
A, We was late.. B, We were late.. C, We be late..

82
00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.262
The answer is B: We were late..

83
00:04:51.417 --> 00:04:54.229
According to the reading, where were the family last week?

84
00:04:54.529 --> 00:04:58.264
A, in Siem Reap. B, at school. C, at work.

85
00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.823
The answer is A: in Siem Reap.

86
00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:08.057
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:08.917 --> 00:05:10.452
Where were you yesterday?

88
00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.715
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:21.015 --> 00:05:35.562
Yesterday I was at home in the morning, and I was at school in the afternoon. My friends were at school too. We were tired, but we were happy. I use was with I and were with we or they.

90
00:05:35.862 --> 00:05:37.861
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:42.830
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past of be: was and were.

92
00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:47.129
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:05:47.429 --> 00:05:50.395
See you in Unit twenty-seven. Goodbye!

94
00:05:50.695 --> 00:05:53.754
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

